<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-7">
        <div class="rc-card">
            <div class="rc-card-head">
                <h2>Something went wrong</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4">
                <p>
                    <i class="bi bi-exclamation-octagon text-danger fs-4 align-middle" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="align-middle ms-2">
                        That request failed. The details are in the application log with the request
                        id, which is where they belong — an error page is the wrong place to print
                        a connection string or a query.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class="rc-help mb-4">
                    If a run was in progress it is unaffected: runs checkpoint per step and resume
                    from the last completed one rather than starting over.
                </p>
                <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">
                    Back to the dashboard
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
